# `power::Measurements`

A set of measurements with their values and accuracies.

## Signature

```cpp
power::Measurements
```

## What It Does

The data of one estimation: which quantity each measurement is, where it was taken, its value and its standard deviation. The values and standard deviations may carry leading scenario axes.

## Fields

| Field | Meaning | Default |
|---|---|---|
| `kind` | The `MeasureKind` of each measurement. | required |
| `index` | The bus or line each measurement belongs to. | required |
| `value` | The measured values, `[..., measurement]`; angles in radians and powers per unit. | required |
| `stddev` | The standard deviation of each value, `[..., measurement]`; strictly positive. | required |

## Returns

A value; validated by `estimate`.

## Errors

Fewer measurements than unknowns, a non-positive standard deviation, an index outside its family, or unequal lengths are rejected.

## Interpretation and Use

The estimate trusts a measurement in inverse proportion to its standard deviation, so give the real accuracy of each instrument. The measurements may be listed in any order.

